<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="11">
<name>Control System</name>
<section id="10033_S0007" variety="S0007">
<name>CAN Communication</name>
<ttl id="10033_S0007_741KB_T000K" variety="T000K">
<name>CAN Communication System</name>
<para id="RM000000N9R00BX" category="J" type-id="30391" name-id="950US-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Steering Angle Sensor Communication Stop Mode</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000N9R00BX_01" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AD00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Diagnosis Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Suspected Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Steering Angle Sensor Communication Stop Mode</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>"Steering Angle Sensor" is not displayed on the "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" screen of TaSCAN</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Corresponds to 'steering angle sensor communication stop mode' in the DTC combination table</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>(1) (1)' open circuit or connector</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Steering sensor (steering angle sensor) power source system malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Steering sensor (steering angle sensor) internal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000N9R00BX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AE00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162428J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000N9R00BX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AF00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When measuring the resistance of the CAN bus, turn the IG OFF, confirm that warning functions such as the key reminder warning system are not operating, and leave the vehicle for 1 minutes or more without operating the key or switches or opening/closing the doors before starting measurement. If it is necessary to open a door during inspection, open it beforehand.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When inspecting each connector, before disconnecting it, push the connector case in the connecting direction and check that the connector is not loose or disconnected.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When disconnecting a connector, check that the connector terminals and connector case are free of damage, deformation, corrosion, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000N9R00BX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AG00000">
<testtitle>CAN Bus Open Circuit Inspection (Steering Angle Sensor Branch Line)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the ignition switch OFF and disconnect the vehicle harness connector from the steering sensor (steering angle sensor).</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146385J05" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the steering sensor (steering angle sensor) vehicle harness connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>3(CANH) - 2(CANL)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>54 to 69Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0002" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0004" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00000AH00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (Sensor Power Source Circuit)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance and voltage between each terminal of the steering sensor and body ground.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C146385J06" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<atten3>
<ptxt>With the connector connected, inspect from the back of the connector.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 (ESS) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG OFF</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.94in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.16in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4 (IG1) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>5 (BAT) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>11 to 14V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0003" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0005" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0003">
<testtitle>Replace Steering Sensor<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000003059000X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0004">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Branch Wire or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000N9R00BX_04_0005">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
